        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Inserting `\\t` in multiple places within the snippet reduces its readability.\n\nI don't quite agree. On the contrary, it makes snippet more readable in a sense that it makes it clearer of what the end result is going to be. And all snippet collections I know use `\\t` to indicate relative indent.\n\n> Could you implement a feature that allows users to indent each level with 2 spaces? You can automatically adjust the indentation when the snippet has been expanded based on the buffer settings, such as using tabs or 4 spaces instead of 2.\n\nIf this is only about not wanting to explicitly use `\\t`, then this is not a good design (explicit `\\t` is). If it is about something that can not be solved with explicit `\\t` and is not currently implemented, then I don't understand the issue and an exact example would help.",
            "created_at": "2025-04-28T16:31:24Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1650#issuecomment-2835828860",
