            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It is so the body can look like the first example. The second one is not clear to read and harder to write.\n> \n> ```\n> {\n>   \"  1\",\n>   \"    2\",\n>   \"      3\",\n>   \"        4\",\n> }\n> \n> {\n>   \"\\t1\",\n>   \"\\t\\t2\",\n>   \"\\t\\t\\t3\",\n>   \"\\t\\t\\t\\t4\",\n> }\n> ```\n\nNo, sorry, the second one is the recommended approach to have \"adjustable\" indent ([as documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1021)). The first one hard codes indent width as two spaces and there is no clear/straightforward/robust way to make this kind of syntax transform into tab characters in case of 'noexpandtab'.",
